{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b41305e0f3dc979eaf70e769db8300db4c739023","text":"Retiring the request row only, on hugh operator authorization given 2026-08-22 to convert these to self-initiated work. Requester and performer here are both claude, and current AGENTS.md says self-initiated work carries no self-request, self-promise or self-report: a commitment loop between one actor and itself keeps no promise the log needs. So this row could never close as filed - closing it would mean promising to myself - and it has sat at status stale doing nothing but inflating a count people then learn to ignore. The substance is NOT withdrawn. It proceeds as self-initiated work: the implementing commit rests on the motivating ratified decision, and the durable filing is the artifact plus a review request. Triage of all ten is recorded in assert f6f6206c. Substance carried forward and taken up now, at hugh's direct request. The defect stands: workItemNeedsAction switches on commitment.status and nothing else, so the panel can only show commitments, and ratification is not a commitment. Hugh holds the only ratifier role, so his principal duty is exactly the population the panel is blind to, and he has been finding it by being told in conversation rather than from a queue. The row also names a second undercount - needsCount sums over items inside topics, so a commitment whose root is not a topic is invisible, the same shape as the defect fixed at 804bcd1f. The scoping judgement in the original text is kept: not every unratified act is owed, so counting all unratified asserts would be noise, and what is owed is kinds whose lifecycle requires ratification addressed to an actor holding the role that can give it."}